      "label": "The editor's end-to-end tests now run one file at a time",
      "excerpt": "The editor's end-to-end tests now run one file at a time",
      "text": "Maybe change to `unit tests` and `integration tests` -- and integration tests run separately?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-08T20:44:12.339Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-08T20:45:45.927Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes, and it fixes a real cost. Today the tests that drive a running editor are inside the app folder's plain test command, so with an editor running that command takes about 15 minutes longer.</p>\n<p>What I'll do, once the agent on I8 is finished (it's changing the same test setup):</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><b>Unit tests:</b> everything that needs no running editor. The usual test command runs only these, and so does the finishing pass.</li>\n  <li><b>Integration tests:</b> the 23 files that drive the running editor, one at a time. They get their own command, <code>yarn test:integration</code>, and the test set is renamed from <code>app:editor</code> to <code>app:integration</code>.</li>\n  <li>The tests that run in a real browser without the editor count as unit tests.</li>\n  <li>CI doesn't change: it has no running editor, so these files skip there already.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Queued as a todo. Say so here if you'd rather have other names.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
